1	line	Outlaw	Okay... Good luck with that...
1	line	Mudfoot	Me no understand. Why no work?
1	line	Captain Harlan	What's happening here? What's all the commotion?
1	cond	If the player didn't speak with Captain Harlan with Mudfoot before:
2	line	Captain Harlan	A goblin? Is this the one responsible for the robbery, adventurer?
2	line	Player	As it turns out, no. Mudfoot here is actually trying to deal with the thieves as well.
2	action	continue
1	cond	If the player spoke with Captain Harlan with Mudfoot before:
2	line	Captain Harlan	Adventurer? You still have that goblin with you. What's going on?
2	line	Player	Well, as it turns out, Mudfoot here is actually trying to deal with the thieves as well.
2	action	continue
1	line	Captain Harlan	He is?
1	line	Mudfoot	Yes. Nasty humans try to frame innocent goblins. Me here to stop them. Me make them go dead.
1	line	Captain Harlan	You killed them?
1	line	Player	Not yet. Mudfoot seems to be having some... difficulties with that.
1	line	Captain Harlan	I see... In that case, come. Let us discuss this further.
1	line	Captain Harlan	Right, regarding these thieves... You said that your goblin friend wasn't able to kill them?
1	line	Mudfoot	Me try hit them with big hammer, but it no work.
1	line	Captain Harlan	I see. Did they have armour?
1	line	Player	Yes, the armour of a ranger.
1	line	Mudfoot	Yes, ranger. Other goblins tell me rangers die best when you hit them up close. That what me do. Go close and big smack.
1	line	Captain Harlan	Ah... Tell me... Mudfoot... have you heard of something called the combat triangle?
1	line	Mudfoot	Triangle? Like roof?
1	line	Captain Harlan	Yes, sometimes...
1	line	Captain Harlan	Anyway, when those goblin friends of yours told you that melee works best against a ranger, that's what they were referring to.
1	line	Mudfoot	But why triangle?
1	line	Captain Harlan	Well, melee often works best against an opponent using ranged, ranged typically works best when fighting an opponent using magic, and magic is normally the best option when fighting someone using melee.
1	line	Mudfoot	But that what me do. Me do the close up hit. Why no work?
1	line	Captain Harlan	The combat triangle isn't the only thing to consider when taking on a foe. The way that you're attacking is also important. Take melee for example. You have crushing attacks, slashing attacks and stabbing attacks.
1	line	Mudfoot	Oh, me like to do big crush best. That why me have big hammer.
1	line	Captain Harlan	Indeed, but the armour typically worn by a ranger is quite resilient to crushing attacks. You'll likely find you have better luck with a stabbing attack instead.
1	line	Captain Harlan	Of course, for that, you'll need the right weapon. As you've already noted, something like a warhammer works well for crushing, but if your aim is to stab, a weapon like a dagger or shortsword will work best.
1	line	Mudfoot	So me go get big poker, then nasty bow man die?
1	line	Captain Harlan	Well, there are no guarantees of course, but it will definitely improve your odds.
1	line	Mudfoot	Yes... Me know all this already of course. Me just pretended not to so trusty human sidekick can do learning. Me know human afraid to ask for help.
1	line	Player	That's not-
1	line	Mudfoot	It okay though. This why human sidekick and me in charge.
1	line	Player	Hmm... Shall we go and find that outlaw and try again?
1	line	Mudfoot	Yes! They go north towards that windmill. Me go grab poker and meet sidekick there. You make sure you grab poker as well.
1	line	Captain Harlan	I can sort you out with a suitable weapon if needed, adventurer. Alternatively, the local blacksmith should be able to sell you one, or give you some advice on making your own.
1	line	Mudfoot	Weapon good. No steal one though. Stealing bad, as Mudfoot always say, apart from when it okay, which isn't now.
1	line	Player	Words to live by... Anything else we should grab before we do this?
1	line	Captain Harlan	Given you're going into a fight, some food would be wise.
1	line	Mudfoot	This true. Food make you feel better if you get hit, but me never get hit, so me never need food.
1	line	Player	If you say so.
1	line	Mudfoot	Okay, time to go now.
1	box	Mudfoot departs.
1	line	Captain Harlan	It seems you know what you need to do next. Good luck, adventurer.
